  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its excessive depth, height and siting along the common boundary with number 36 Monroe Crescent, would result in an overly dominant form of development which would lead to an unneighbourly loss of outlook, sunlight and daylight as perceived from neighbouring property, and result in an unacceptably heightened sense of enclosure. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and policy DMD11 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
